From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:23:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winegcc: align ARM64 and ARM64EC builtins to 16 KiB sections

winegcc links ARM64 and ARM64EC modules with 64 KiB section alignment,
and the file alignment follows it. On iOS every pseudo-process copies
each builtin it loads into the JIT pool, and the copy includes the
padding: kernel32's copy took 960 KiB for 400 KiB of sections. In the
RDR2 play that ran the pool's head out (PLA-377), 154.7 MiB of the 535
MiB live were that padding.

The default for these targets is now 0x4000, the phone's page, for
both the section and the file alignment. Wine's unix loader maps an
image whose sections are aligned to at least the host page as usual, and
a writable section now starts on a page of its own, so the pool copy
needs no data-align shift. winebuild's data-only modules have no code
and get no copy; they are unchanged.

Linear: PLA-377
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-19-smaller-image-copies.md
Offered-upstream: no; the 16 KiB alignment is for the iOS port's JIT pool
---
 tools/winegcc/winegcc.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c b/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c
index 0d8586e..5f5c475 100644
--- a/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c
+++ b/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c
@@ -2015,8 +2015,11 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
     if (is_pe) use_msvcrt = true;
     if (output && strendswith( output, ".fake" )) fake_module = true;
 
+    /* iOS (PLA-377): every process copies each ARM64 and ARM64EC builtin it
+     * loads into the JIT pool, padding and all, so they are aligned to the
+     * phone's 16 KiB page instead of 64 KiB. */
     if (!section_align)
-        section_align = (target.cpu == CPU_ARM64 || target.cpu == CPU_ARM64EC) ? "0x10000" : "0x1000";
+        section_align = (target.cpu == CPU_ARM64 || target.cpu == CPU_ARM64EC) ? "0x4000" : "0x1000";
 
     if (!file_align) file_align = section_align;
 
